// - The task asks for symbolic math expressions - the parser should accept
//   standard arithmetic expressions with variable names
//
// This approach ensures:
// - Spans are always opened (prefixBudget forces entry)
// - Span content is parser-controlled (no LaTeX/backtick contamination)
// - Spans are closed (managed helper handles completeness-gated close)
// - Budget is respected (maxSteps cap)
//
// Guidance emphasizes: write reasoning outside spans, put ONLY the final
// numeric/symbolic answer expression inside << >>, no LaTeX, no backticks,
// no template syntax.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity:
//   GenerateWithPrefixAndManagedSpan's postcondition guarantees:
//   !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//   Both invariant branches are discharged by the helper's own proof.
//
// progress:
//   GenerateWithPrefixAndManagedSpan has postcondition:
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps
//   and cost <= maxSteps (via the helper's internal step counter).
//   The helper consumes at most maxSteps token-steps total, so both the
